# probes-suite-crashes-bricscad — the probes/ suite dies on BricsCAD before any record

STATUS: OPEN. Found 2026-08-30, the first time the probes/ suite was ever
pointed at BricsCAD.

## Symptom

On BOTH platforms the results file contains exactly one line:

    ((KIND . "wrapper-start"))

and nothing else. The wrapper opened the file, wrote its marker, and the
engine died before a single probe record — before even the run-start
that CAD-PROBE-BEGIN-RUN writes.

    macOS   (BricsCAD V26)      Segmentation fault: 11, runner exit 139
    Windows (BricsCAD V25 fr_FR) silent exit, run-probes reports
                                 "the wrapper started but never reached
                                  its end record"

AutoCAD ran the same wrapper, the same six suites, to completion. So did
the clautolisp baseline.

## Why it had never been seen

There was no CI job for this suite on BricsCAD at all — only AutoCAD —
and on a macOS workstation `make probe` could not FIND BricsCAD
(issues/closed/probe-detect-cad-misses-macos-bricscad.issue), so it
silently ran the clautolisp baseline instead. Between them, the suite had
simply never met the engine.

## What is known and what is not

The wrapper LOADS all six suite files and only then runs them, so the
death is in a LOAD or in CAD-PROBE-BEGIN-RUN, not in a probe body. That
is as far as the evidence goes. In particular it is NOT yet known whether
the fatal file is one of the four original suites or probe-foreach-scope
(added the same day), because they all load before anything runs.

PROBE_SUITES (added with this ticket) is what settles it: it narrows the
wrapper to named suites, so each can be tried alone. The BricsCAD jobs
now run `PROBE_SUITES=foreach-scope`, which both answers the question
that is actually open and performs half the experiment.

## Next

  - If foreach-scope alone RUNS: the fatal suite is one of the original
    four; bisect them the same way.
  - If foreach-scope alone DIES: the new file is implicated and should be
    reduced until it does not.

Either way the full suite should be restored on BricsCAD, and the
narrowing in .gitlab/native.yml removed, once the cause is known.

## The general point, again

`make probe` falls back to the clautolisp baseline when it detects no
CAD, and a suite that dies leaves a file behind. Both are good designs —
and both mean a run can SUCCEED at the shell level while measuring
nothing. The results themselves say which product answered; nothing else
does.
